  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will be introduced to quadratic expressions in vertex form and learn that this form allows us to easily see where the vertex of a graph is located.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Recognize the "vertex form" of a quadratic equation.</item>
  <item>Relate the numbers in the vertex form of a quadratic equation to its graph.</item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item>7.15.1: Analyzing Two Sets of Equations</item>
  <item>7.15.2: The Vertex Form
    <list>
      <item>7.15.2: Self Check</item>
      <item>7.15.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
 </item>
  <item>7.15.3: The Coordinates of the Vertex <list>
    <item>7.15.3: Self Check</item>
    <item>7.15.3: Additional Resources</item>
  </list></item>
 
  <item>7.15.4: The Graph of a Function in Vertex Form</item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review.</emphasis></para>
<list>
  <item>7.15.5: Practice</item>
  <item>7.15.6: Lesson Summary</item>
</list></section>
</content>
